Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] arm64: dts: qcom: Vivobook S15: disable Linux ADSP

Diagnostic analogue of Johan's CRD CXSD WIP tip:
a62d82531b37804f4b4f8041271f6478adedad0a.
https://github.com/jhovold/linux/commit/a62d82531b37804f4b4f8041271f6478adedad0a

Not a daily-use fix. Disables Linux ADSP startup, audio, battmgr and other
ADSP GLINK services. It does NOT guarantee that boot firmware's lite ADSP
has been shut down: a disabled PAS driver cannot perform the lite PAS
shutdown done during a normal load. A null result is therefore ambiguous.
Use AOP MMIO residency counters rather than ADSP battery/APSS data for
this diagnostic boot. Keep a known-good boot entry and arrange manual wake.
Unreviewed, not compiled or hardware tested. CDSP remains unchanged.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
 	firmware-name = "qcom/x1e80100/ASUSTeK/vivobook-s15/qcadsp8380.mbn",
 			"qcom/x1e80100/ASUSTeK/vivobook-s15/adsp_dtbs.elf";
 
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &remoteproc_cdsp {
